 ### Two-stage training for proposers
-A training schedule split into two equal-duration phases to stabilize learning of a trainable proposer network in NeRF-ID [S22, unofficial]. In Phase 1, the learnt proposer is trained to mimic the heuristic proposer by minimizing the L2 matching loss between their proposal sets [S22, unofficial]. In Phase 2, all network components are trained end-to-end. At the start of this phase, the optimizer state is reset and a linear warmup for 1,000 steps is performed to reduce shock from switching regimes [S22, unofficial]. Training from scratch sometimes works but often fails; two-stage training is consistently effective [S22, unofficial].
